WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:10.030
2018 is here and incredibly enough, the Earth's
core hasn't melted down yet.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:15.260
Somehow, humanity has managed to survive several
extinction level events over the past few

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:21.210
weeks, including but not limited to, the republican
tax bill passing, net neutrality being repealed,

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:25.480
Russian bots trolling Twitter, and of course,
late night Trump Tweets.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:30.350
While it's pretty clear the endless hysteria
about the return of the Nazis, the hyperbole

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:35.400
describing the end of the world and the general
lunacy of our collective social media hive

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:41.570
mind is going to continue into 2018 and beyond,
I want to look back, make my prediction and

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:42.980
offer a glimmer of hope in the madness.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:48.969
In my first Direct Message of 2017, I had
said if 2016 was the year of fake outrage,

00:00:48.969 --> 00:00:52.609
then 2017 would be the year of misguided anger.

00:00:52.609 --> 00:00:56.890
Though I'm no Nostradamus, I think my prediction
came out looking pretty damn good.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:02.059
My prediction was based on a few trends, but
primarily that if you spend all of 2016 saying

00:01:02.059 --> 00:01:06.860
that Trump was Hitler, and he turned out not
to be Hitler, that you would've painted yourself

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:12.369
into an intellectual corner, which could only
come out in misguided anger.

00:01:12.369 --> 00:01:17.920
Once you've labeled someone as Hitler, you
can't really walk your statement back by acknowledging

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:21.040
that they might occasionally do something
good.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:25.030
This line of thinking was a trap that the
Left set for itself and is one of the reasons

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:29.649
I spent so much time in 2016 trying to reform
the Left.

00:01:29.649 --> 00:01:34.630
The endless name calling and virtue signaling
was obviously going to lead to more misguided

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:39.579
anger if the prophecy of Trump as Hitler didn't
come true.

00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:44.659
After all, you can never give a Hitler figure
credit if he does something good, so you just

00:01:44.659 --> 00:01:49.899
have to endlessly double-down and slide further
and further to the extreme.

00:01:49.899 --> 00:01:55.200
You may hate Trump's appointees, the Republican
tax plan and more, but you do have to face

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.659
that Hitler he is not.

00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:02.810
To continue this line of thinking is to dishonor
the millions of people who died at the hands

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.359
of a fanatical madman.

00:02:05.359 --> 00:02:09.800
The misguided anger which Trump's election
brought didn't just affect politicians and

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.080
pundits, but ordinary people, too.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.620
Every single day I get dozens of emails from
regular folks who are losing friends, who

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:21.720
are ostrasized by their family members, or
most dangerously afraid to say what they think

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.209
because it may fall outside of the accepted
narrative.

00:02:25.209 --> 00:02:33.099
News organizations from Buzzfeed to HuffPo
even to CNN and the NY Times, exposed themselves

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:39.680
as places of Leftists activism more than places
of honest and unbiased journalism.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.580
While the 2016 election should've brought
some introspection amongst this class, it

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:50.190
instead brought a doubling down of attacking
anyone who steps outside of the accepted norms.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:55.220
This dishonesty and desire to control what
you think is exactly what led to the rise

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:58.850
of the trolls, the meme makers and the frogs.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:00.440
OK, on to 2018.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:05.330
While there clearly will be no course correction
by those who trade in identity politics and

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:09.120
collectivism, I see many signs that their
movement is beginning to lose steam.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.129
Of course if you were tracking this all along
you knew this was the inevitability of the

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:18.280
oppression olympics, if you believe victimhood
to be virtue, then you must be always be a

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.710
bigger victim than the person next to you.

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:25.390
This is the fatal flaw of intersectionality:
together you aren't stronger, you are actually

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:28.220
weaker because of your competing interests.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:32.269
This is why leftism, collectivism, socialism
or whatever you want to call it has always

00:03:32.269 --> 00:03:37.900
led to more authoritarian control and more
dead bodies in the name of tolerance.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:43.099
It is a snake that eats its tail, and right
now if you look close enough, the snake is

00:03:43.099 --> 00:03:45.439
about half way through with lunch.

00:03:45.439 --> 00:03:50.160
While the snake eats, those of us who are
woke, as the kids say, are going to find allies

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.989
every which way we look.

00:03:51.989 --> 00:03:56.440
Right before Christmas I spoke at the largest
gathering of conservative college students

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:01.250
ever, at Turning Point USA's annual conference
in Palm Springs.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:05.690
Many former Rubin Report guests were there
including Ben Shapiro, Dennis Prager and Greg

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:06.690
Gutfeld.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:10.810
During my speech I talked about being for
gay marriage, for a woman's right to choose

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:14.340
and a slew of other so-called liberal ideas.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:19.090
The speech wasn't just warmly received, I
actually got a standing ovation for talking

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:22.560
about our differences and how we can find
common ground.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:27.600
I'd be happy to do the same exact speech for
a progressive organization, but I won't hold

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.950
my breath waiting for the invitation.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:35.900
While one side preaches tolerance but doesn't
actually practice it, I think 2018 is finally

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:40.169
going to be the year this script gets torn
up and rewritten.

00:04:40.169 --> 00:04:44.600
If you truly stand for the individual and
believe we live in a free society where our

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:50.270
differences should be relished and not relinquished,
then you will find people to connect with

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:55.550
every direction -- just look at the diverse
voices who we had in this very studio who

00:04:55.550 --> 00:05:02.030
caught fire in 2017, like Jordan Peterson,
Brett Weinstein, Lindsay Shepard, Laci Green,

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:04.780
Colin Moriarty and Yasmine Muhammed.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:10.110
These people came from all across the physical
map as well as the ideological map, yet have

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:16.150
found common cause in fighting for their ability
to say and think what they believe.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:22.450
So if 2016 was the year of Fake Outrage and
2017 was the Year of Misguided Anger, I believe

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:26.500
that 2018 will be the year of Unusual Alliances.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:32.330
If you make the decision in your mind to be
for the only diversity that matters, the diversity

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:37.190
of thought, you will quickly find it easy
to find friends where you once found enemies.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:43.910
And, as has happened to me on more than one
occasion, you might just change your mind

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:46.440
instead of changes someone elses.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:51.870
It can be humbling and even scary when that
happens, but that's the risk of real diversity,

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.670
but I think it's one well worth taking.

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:57.800
My challenge to you is to do something this
year.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.610
Don't just talk about it, do it.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.680
Whatever that is to you.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:09.020
Start fighting for your beliefs in the real
world, not just by using a hash tag on Twitter.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:15.120
Even if you disagree with me on everything,
get out there and fight for whatever it is

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.599
you believe.

00:06:16.599 --> 00:06:21.030
Obviously don't use violence or your right
to free speech to infringe on someone else's

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:26.250
right to use theirs, but stand up for the
ideas you care about.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:31.380
The old systems of politics, media, Hollywood
and even sports are crumbling right before

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:35.449
our eyes and it's up to us to decide what
will come next.

00:06:35.449 --> 00:06:40.690
I believe that we have a chance to build on
the ideas of classical liberalism, of libertarianism,

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:47.889
of individualism and of personal freedom instead
of authoritarianism, socialism leftism and

00:06:47.889 --> 00:06:49.520
authoritarian control.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:54.360
I will fight for those ideas like never before
in 2018 and I hope that you will join me,

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:55.000
whatever that means to you...

